<div class="card gap">
	<div class="eyebrow">The gap</div>
	<h2>You were told AI would change everything. So far it's just changed your budget.</h2>
	<p>
		You bought the tools. Sent the team to the webinars. Maybe even hired a consultant. And you still
		can't answer the only question that matters: did any of it make us money? Is our marketing
		generating more leads?
	</p>
	<p>
		You're not alone. MIT found 95% of corporate AI projects return nothing. Not because the tech is
		broken, but because it gets aimed at the wrong problem by people who don't understand the business
		underneath it. Meanwhile the clock runs, competitors inch ahead, and "AI" quietly becomes a line
		item you'd rather not explain.
	</p>
</div>

<div class="card solution">
	<div class="eyebrow">Solution</div>
	<h2>That's the gap I close.</h2>
	<p>
		I'm not a technologist selling software. I'm an operator who's built and run twelve companies
		across every department there is, and went deep on AI the day it arrived. I start with your
		business, find the one or two places AI actually moves profit, and prove the return. No science
		projects. No hype. You stop guessing at AI and start getting paid by it.
	</p>
</div>

